From f947435dbbb714a6ca42dc7cd06f74443b0d1bf2 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Wed, 14 Oct 2026 03:16:11 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 05/12] gated delta rule: fused path on Vulkan (host-shared
 memory) and Metal

Vulkan and Metal had no fused Gated DeltaNet: callers ran the tensor path, one op per token
step. Under MoltenVK every op is a GPU round trip (~0.8 ms on the macos-15 runner) and the
tensor path was 11x (prefill) / 3x (decode) slower than the CPU kernel even on lavapipe.

- Vulkan devices whose tensors live in host-shared memory (VulkanDevice::host_shared_memory:
  integrated / unified GPUs such as Apple Silicon under MoltenVK, CPU devices such as
  lavapipe) run the CPU kernel (the test oracle) on host copies of the tensors.
- Metal: conv, SiLU, q / k L2 norms and the q scale in tensor ops, then a native scan kernel
  (one thread per value column, the state column in thread memory, q / k staged in
  threadgroup memory, gates computed in place). A device enables it only after a self-check
  against the CPU kernel (conv and recurrent state given, GQA); otherwise the tensor path.
- delta_rule_tests: the GPU cases also run on Metal / Vulkan devices that report support.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
